Subject: [PATCH 5/5] round C1.3b: one brand layer in Outfit for the portal and
 golden /planning

Tao, 2026-09-11: unify the brand layer only; body text stays as it is.

- New tokens: --goaa-font-display (= --goaa-font, Outfit first) and
  --goaa-font-body (exactly the golden globals.css body stack).
- Portal: .goaa-portal body text moves from Outfit back to the body stack;
  brand text, eyebrow, h1/h2, rail items/CTA/tag, buttons, tabs and
  pp-h1/h2/h3/pp-btn/pp-tab use the display font.
- Golden /planning: .goaa-brand, + New, rail label/items/NEW tag, kickers,
  workspace section/plan titles and the Matters heading use the display
  font. Chat bubbles, composer, plan text and footer are unchanged.
- globals.css and butler-workspace.css are untouched; the rules live at the
  end of the token sheets so they win over the existing `font: inherit`
  resets. Reverting this commit restores the C1.2 look exactly.

Measured in Chromium with the shipped woff2: Outfit and the current stack
are within 1-3px on every rail label at 14-16px ("Skills Marketplace"
113 vs 113 at 14px), so the 190px golden rail gains no new wrapping; mock
render shows all five rail items at one line (40px).

Test: scripts/test-brand-font.cjs (5).

